*.pyc
__pycache__/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# muni.db itself is never committed: once 2FA setup completes it also
# holds the live TOTP secret in auth_totp, and once the invoicing feature
# is used it holds real business/payment details (business_profile,
# invoices). The genuinely static, safe-to-ship part — municipalities,
# meetings, packets, blocked_sources — gets exported into the separately
# committed data/muni_seed.db via src/export_seed_db.py instead; a fresh
# deployment copies that in as its starting muni.db and grows its own
# live secrets from there.
data/muni.db
data/muni.db-wal
data/muni.db-shm

# Flask session-signing key — a live security secret, same reasoning as
# muni.db's auth_totp table above.
data/.flask_secret_key

# Runtime logs, not source.
data/*.log

# Uploaded business logo — per-deployment branding, not source.
data/logo.png
data/logo_watermark.png
